WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Chef John's Italian Meatballs. 135 min · 10 servings · Italian

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Ingredients: 15. 1/3 cup plain bread crumbs; 1/2 cup milk or beef broth; 2 tablespoons olive oil; 1 onion, diced

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Step 1. Cover a baking sheet with foil and spray lightly with cooking spray. Soak bread crumbs in milk in a small bowl for 20 minutes.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Step 2. Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Cook and stir onion until onion has softened and is translucent, about 5 minutes. Reduce heat to low an…

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Step 3. Gently stir beef and pork together in a large bowl. Add onions, bread crumb mixture, eggs, ricotta cheese, Parmesan cheese, parsley, garlic, salt, bl…

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step 4. Preheat the oven to 425°F (220°C).

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Step 5. Form mixture into balls about 1 1/2 inches in diameter. Arrange in a single layer on the prepared baking sheet.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step 6. Bake in the preheated oven until browned and cooked through, 15 to 20 minutes.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Step 7. Serve with your favorite tomato sauce. Tip: After baking, add meatballs to tomato sauce and simmer 1 to 2 hours for best flavor.

